    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch03-13: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.52";
    dc:description "Trait matching can be tested for many interaction classes, but joining morphology to interaction records is incomplete and causal coevolution is confounded by shared environments. The universal formulation is beyond current coverage.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Across documented interactions, test whether organismal structures covary with corresponding competitor, predator, prey or escape-related structures after phylogenetic and environmental controls. Reciprocal functional matching supports the relational claim.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'Every organism' and 'most essential' are not exhaustively testable.", "Trait matching does not by itself establish causal shaping.";
